      "full_translation": "And We bestowed upon him Ishaq (Isaac) and Ya'qub (Jacob), each of them We guided; and Nuh (Noah) We guided before; and from his descendants, Dawud (David), Sulayman (Solomon), Ayyub (Job), Yusuf (Joseph), Musa (Moses), and Harun (Aaron). Thus do We reward those who do good. And Zakariya (Zechariah), Yahya (John), 'Isa (Jesus), and Ilyas (Elijah), each one of them was of the righteous. And Isma'il (Ishmael), Al-Yasa' (Elisha), Yunus (Jonah), and Lut (Lot), and each one We preferred over the worlds.",
      "notes": "This is a Quranic verse, hence the translation maintains a formal tone. The term 'progeny' refers to descendants.\nUncertainty Resolution:\n- Resolved:\n  * The term 'ذُرِّيَّتِهِ' is translated as 'descendants' to better reflect the context of lineage.\n  * The diacritics for ذُرِّيَّتِهِ were confirmed based on standard pronunciation and context.",
      "verification_status": "Verified",
      "verification_issues": null
    },
